In-surface bug found AND fixed during verification (this is why the macOS compile pass was run):
  Breadcrumbs.Previews.swift / Breadcrumbs.Tests.swift sample-item builders originally wrote
  `let onNavigate: (@MainActor () -> Void)? = isLast ? nil : {}` — a closure literal inside a
  ternary assigned to an optional @MainActor closure, which trips a Swift type-checker bug
  ("failed to produce diagnostic for expression") under -D DEBUG. The first standalone typecheck
  missed it (no -D DEBUG => the #if DEBUG block was skipped); the in-project macOS build surfaced
  it. Rewritten to a conditional assignment (no closure-in-ternary). DEBUG typecheck now EXIT=0.

