[parity] — web branches reproduced (faithful to components/layout/Breadcrumbs.tsx)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Pure presentational, prop-driven; only hook is useTranslation => NO loading/error/stale/offline
  branch (nothing to fetch/fail/age). Those belong to the host page, exactly as the sibling
  presentational surfaces ActiveFilterChips (0147) + HistoryListRow (0091) documented. Documented
  verbatim in Breadcrumbs.Adapter.swift. Not a scope shortcut.
- hidden: items.length <= 1 -> web `return null`. Native: EmptyView by default; a friendly
  localized placeholder when hideWhenSuppressed == false (never a blank box).
- trail: leading Home link + chevron-separated crumbs.
- per-crumb role: trailing crumb = current-page emphasized text (web isLast); earlier crumb with
  href = link (web <PrefetchLink>); earlier crumb without href = muted text (web !item.href).
- compact width: middle crumbs (web isMiddle, `hidden sm:inline`) collapse behind ONE accessible
  "…" menu — the Apple-idiomatic, VoiceOver-preserving read of the web per-item `…` markers.
- navigation delegated to the host via onNavigate / onHomeNavigate (dependency inversion); the
  surface never rewrites a route itself (web hands routing to react-router).

